\begin{enumerate}
\item Parentheses
\item NOT
\item Multiplicative (*, /)
\item Additive (+, -)
\item Relational (=, <>, <, <=, >, >=)
\item AND
\item OR
\end{enumerate}

\section{Primary Expressions}

Primary expressions are the building blocks of more complex expressions.

\subsection{Numeric Literals}
Example: @code{42}

\subsection{String Literals}
Example: @code{"Hello"}

\subsection{Identifiers}
Example: @code{Count}, @code{Total\$}, @code{\_flag}

\subsection{SELF}
Refers to the current object instance within a method.

\subsection{NULL}
Represents the null object reference.

\subsection{Parenthesized Expressions}
@code{( expression )} groups subexpressions to override precedence.

\section{Number Literal Formats}

This BASIC frontend supports multiple number literal formats:

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Hexadecimal Numbers}: Prefix with @code{\&H} or @code{\&h}. Example: @code{\&HFF} → 255, @code{\&h10} → 16.
\item \textbf{Octal Numbers}: Prefix with @code{\&O} or @code{\&o}. Example: @code{\&O77} → 63, @code{\&o10} → 8.
\item \textbf{Binary Numbers}: Prefix with @code{\&B} or @code{\&b}. Example: @code{\&B1010} → 10, @code{\&b11} → 3.
\item \textbf{Dword (32-bit) Numbers}: Prefix with @code{\&D} or @code{\&d}. Example: @code{\&D4294967295} → 4294967295. Values must be in range 0 to 2^32-1.
\item \textbf{Decimal Numbers}: Default format without prefix. Example: @code{42}, @code{1000}.
\end{itemize}

All numeric formats are converted to their decimal equivalent in the token stream for processing.

\section{Functions}

The BASIC frontend does not provide intrinsic functions beyond those exposed via libraries or OOPS methods. Functions are invoked using `GOSUB` with appropriate targets (library, method, or service). Examples include:

- **Mathematical Functions**: Access via library calls (e.g., `GOSUB "SIN" IN LIBRARY`).
- **String Manipulation**: Similarly via library or object methods.
- **System Calls**: Through service-dispatch mechanisms.

Consult the specific library or class documentation for available functions.

