\end{tabular}

This chapter provides a complete reference for the BASIC frontend language as implemented in EightBol. For further details, consult the lexer and parser source files.

\section{Identifier Normalization}

All identifiers in BASIC programs are automatically normalized to PascalCase format during parsing, before AST node creation. This ensures consistent naming across the generated code.

\subsection{Normalization Rules}
\begin{itemize}
\item Underscores (@code{_}) are treated as word separators.
\item Each word is capitalized (first letter uppercase, remainder lowercase).
\item The normalized identifier is formed by concatenating all capitalized words without separators.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Examples}
\begin{table}
\centering
\begin{tabular}{ll}
Original & Normalized \\
\hline
@code{my_variable} & @code{MyVariable} \\
@code{myVariable} & @code{MyVariable} \\
@code{MY_CONST} & @code{MyCon} (note: each segment capitalized) \\
@code{counter} & @code{Counter} \\
@code{total_sum_value} & @code{TotalSumValue} \\
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

\subsection{Effect on AST}
All identifiers appearing in the abstract syntax tree (AST) have been normalized. This applies to:
\begin{itemize}
\item Variable names in @code{LET}, @code{SET}, @code{MOVE} statements.
\item Loop variables in @code{FOR}/@code{NEXT}.
\item Procedure and method names.
\item Class names.
\item Labels and line number references.
\end{itemize}

This normalization ensures consistent identifier treatment throughout compilation and aids in cross-language and cross-platform consistency.

\section{Unsupported BASIC Commands}

The following Dartmouth BASIC commands and functions are \textbf{not supported} by the EightBol BASIC frontend. Programs using these features will produce compile-time errors. This list is provided to help identify code that requires manual translation or restructuring.

\subsection{Input/Output Commands}

\begin{itemize}
\item @code{INPUT\#} — File input
\item @code{PRINT\#} — File output
\item @code{PRINT USING} — Formatted print
\item @code{OPEN} — Open file for I/O
\item @code{CLOSE} — Close file
\item @code{GET} — Get record from file
\item @code{PUT} — Put record to file
\item @code{FIELD} — Define random-access file field
\end{itemize}

\subsection{String Functions}

\begin{itemize}
\item @code{LEFT\$} — Left substring
\item @code{RIGHT\$} — Right substring
\item @code{MID\$} — Middle substring (both statement and function forms)
\item @code{LEN()} — String length
\item @code{ASC()} — Character to ASCII code
\item @code{CHR\$} — ASCII code to character
\item @code{VAL()} — String to number
\item @code{STR\$} — Number to string
\item @code{INSTR()} — String search
\item @code{STRING\$} — Repeat character
\item @code{SPC()} — Print spaces
\item @code{TAB()} — Print to column
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Mathematical Functions}

\begin{itemize}
\item @code{SIN()} — Sine
\item @code{COS()} — Cosine
\item @code{TAN()} — Tangent
\item @code{ATN()} — Arctangent
\item @code{SQR()} — Square root
\item @code{LOG()} — Natural logarithm (note: LOG is used for fault logging in this frontend)
\item @code{EXP()} — Exponential
\item @code{ABS()} — Absolute value
\item @code{SGN()} — Sign function
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Numeric Functions}

\begin{itemize}
\item @code{RND()} — Random number
\item @code{RANDOMIZE} — Seed random number generator
\item @code{INT()} — Integer part (use assignment for truncation)
\item @code{FIX()} — Integer part (truncate toward zero)
\item @code{CINT()} — Convert to integer
\item @code{CSNG()} — Convert to single precision
\item @code{CDbl()} — Convert to double precision
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Memory and Hardware Functions}

\begin{itemize}
\item @code{PEEK()} — Read memory
\item @code{POKE} — Write memory
\item @code{WAIT} — Hardware wait
\item @code{DEEK()} — Read 16-bit memory (some BASIC variants)
\item @code{DOKE} — Write 16-bit memory (some BASIC variants)
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Graphics and Sound Commands}

\begin{itemize}
\item @code{CLS} — Clear screen
\item @code{COLOR} — Set color
\item @code{PLOT} — Plot point
\item @code{DRAW} — Draw graphics
\item @code{CIRCLE} — Draw circle
\item @code{SOUND} — Play sound
\item @code{MUSIC} — Play music
\item @code{PLAY} — Play music sequence
\item @code{VOLUME} — Set volume
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Control Flow Commands}

\begin{itemize}
\item @code{ON ... GOTO} — Computed GOTO (use IF/GOTO instead)
\item @code{ON ... GOSUB} — Computed GOSUB (use IF/GOSUB instead)
\item @code{SELECT CASE} — Multi-way branch (use IF/ELSE IF instead)
\item @code{CONT} — Continue program
\item @code{END IF} — Explicit IF block end
\item @code{NEXT} with multiple variables — not supported
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Program Structure Commands}

\begin{itemize}
\item @code{DIM} — Dimension array (use COPY books for data structures)
\item @code{ERASE} — Erase array
\item @code{READ} — Read from DATA statement
\item @code{DATA} — Data storage
\item @code{RESTORE} — Restore DATA pointer
\item @code{DEF FN} — User-defined functions
\item @code{EXIT FOR} — Exit FOR loop early (use GOTO instead)
\item @code{EXIT DO} — Exit DO loop early (use GOTO instead)
\end{itemize}

\subsection{File I/O Commands}

\begin{itemize}
\item @code{FILES} — List files (directory)
\item @code{LOAD} — Load program
\item @code{SAVE} — Save program
\item @code{RUN} — Run program
\item @code{CHAIN} — Chain to another program
\item @code{MERGE} — Merge programs
\item @code{NEW} — New program (shell command, not program statement)
\item @code{LIST} — List program (shell command, not program statement)
\end{itemize}

\subsection{System Commands}

\begin{itemize}
\item @code{CLEAR} — Clear variables
\item @code{CLR} — Clear variables (abbreviation)
\item @code{CONT} — Continue execution
\item @code{SYSTEM} — Return to operating system
\item @code{SWAP} — Swap variable values
\item @code{POKE} — Memory write
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Operator Overloading and Advanced Features}

\begin{itemize}
\item @code{TYPE} — User-defined data types
\item @code{POKE} — Memory modification
\item @code{CALL} — Assembly routine call (use GOSUB with library instead)
\item @code{USR()} — User-defined machine language function
\end{itemize}

\section{Canonical AST Conformance}

The BASIC frontend parser is conformant to the EIGHTBOL canonical Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) specification. All language constructs map directly to their AST equivalents:

\begin{table}
\centering
\begin{tabular}{ll}
BASIC Statement/Expression & Canonical AST Node \\
\hline
LET @code{var} = @code{expr} & @code{(:move :from expr :to var)} \\
SET @code{var} TO @code{expr} & @code{(:move :from expr :to var)} \\
PCOPY @code{src}, @code{dest}, @code{len} & @code{(:string-blt :from src :to dest :length len)} \\
@code{A}(@code{index}) (subscript) & @code{(:subscript A index)} \\
@code{A}$(@code{start}, @code{length}) & @code{(:refmod :base A$ :start start :length length)} \\
@code{slot} OF @code{object} & @code{(:of slot object)} \\
VARPTR(@code{var}) & @code{(:address-of var)} \\
@code{expr1} AND @code{expr2} & @code{(:bit-and expr1 expr2)} \\
@code{expr1} OR @code{expr2} & @code{(:bit-or expr1 expr2)} \\
@code{expr1} XOR @code{expr2} & @code{(:bit-xor expr1 expr2)} \\
NOT @code{expr} & @code{(:bit-not expr)} \\
NULL & @code{:null} (literal) \\
SELF & @code{:self} (literal) \\
NULL(@code{expr}) & @code{(:null expr)} (test) \\
RETURN & @code{(:goback)} \\
END & @code{(:goback)} \\
@code{expr1} * @code{expr2} & @code{(:× expr1 expr2)} \\
@code{expr1} / @code{expr2} & @code{(:÷ expr1 expr2)} \\
PRINT @code{expr-list} & @code{(:print :expressions expr-list)} \\
INPUT @code{var-list} & @code{(:input :variables var-list)} \\
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

\subsection{Feature Omissions}

The following BASIC features are intentionally omitted:

\begin{itemize}
\item Exponentiation operator (@code{^}) — Use POW(@code{x}, @code{y}) library call instead
\item Shift operators — Not currently implemented; may be added in future versions
\end{itemize}

\section{Translation Notes}

When porting BASIC code to EightBol BASIC:

\begin{enumerate}
\item \textbf{File I/O}: Replace file operations with COPY book mechanisms or service calls
\item \textbf{String manipulation}: Use COBOL-style STRING and UNSTRING via EightBol's COBOL features
\item \textbf{Math functions}: Implement via library calls (GOSUB ... IN LIBRARY)
\item \textbf{Random numbers}: Use service-dispatch random number generators
\item \textbf{Arrays}: Use COBOL data structures defined in COPY books
\item \textbf{Graphics/Sound}: Access via service calls to platform-specific implementations
\item \textbf{ON GOTO/GOSUB}: Rewrite as IF/THEN chains or computed GOTO using IF/GOTO
\end{enumerate}
